<title>SINGAPORE: India cancels one-year naphtha term sell tender.</title>
<headline>India cancels one-year naphtha term sell tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has cancelled a one-year tender to sell 275,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha from Cochin, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>IOC officials were unavailable to comment on reasons for the cancellation of the tender which closed on August 29.</p>
<p>The tender offered 11 cargoes of 25,000 tonnes each from Cochin on India's southwest coast, starting from September.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
